{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation detail for this story (the description carries the decisions).\n\n### (5) Import-convention scans → ruff (`ruff==0.16.3`, `pyproject.toml:257`; verified on the venv's 0.16.2)\n\nCurrent `[tool.ruff.lint]` (`pyproject.toml:437-495`) selects no TID codes; `ignore` must stay the RUF trio and no `extend-ignore` (`tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py:76-107`), so TID goes in `select` + `per-file-ignores` only. TID251 and TID253 are each ONE global list toggled per path, so at most one scoped rule per code can be expressed.\n\n| test module | rule | ruff expression or STAYS |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py::test_no_tests_rooted_imports_anywhere_under_tests` (:57-76, bug a371) | no `tests.`-rooted import anywhere under tests/ | FOLD: `select += [\"TID251\"]`; `[tool.ruff.lint.flake8-tidy-imports.banned-api]` `\"tests\".msg = \"tests.-rooted imports resolve only with the repo root on sys.path, which the bare pytest console script (make test, CI) does not provide; import same-directory helpers by bare name (bug a371)\"`. Parent matching covers `import tests.x`, `from tests import x`, `from tests.x import y`, and in-function imports (verified). Keep `test_audit_page_modules_collect_under_bare_pytest` (the bug's repro) |\n| `tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py::test_no_core_module_imports_heavy_stack_at_module_scope` (:131-148) | no module-scope heavy import under src/rebar except `_engine` | FOLD: `select += [\"TID253\"]`; `[tool.ruff.lint.flake8-tidy-imports]` `banned-module-level-imports = [\"langchain\",\"langgraph\",\"langchain_anthropic\",\"langchain_openai\",\"langchain_mcp_adapters\",\"langfuse\",\"anthropic\",\"deepagents\",\"opentelemetry\",\"pydantic_ai\",\"httpx\",\"tree_sitter\",\"tree_sitter_language_pack\",\"hcl2\",\"lark\"]`; per-file-ignores: `\"src/rebar/_engine/**\" = [\"TID253\"]`, extend `:536` to `\"tests/**\" = [\"T201\", \"TID253\"]` and `:578` to `\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\", \"TID253\"]`. Keep `test_lean_workflow_runtime_pulls_no_heavy_stack`, reading its list from pyproject via `tomllib` so the list has one source. Both rules are green on the current tree (verified with `--config` overrides) |\n| `tests/unit/test_no_reducer_engine_support_cycle.py` (71) | reducer must not module-import `rebar._engine_support` | STAYS: TID253 is claimed by the heavy-stack rule and its scope (all src) differs from this one (reducer only); per-file-ignores cannot scope two lists under one code |\n| `tests/unit/test_scripts_import_convention.py` (184, bug 291e) | sibling import preceded by a `__file__`-derived `sys.path.insert` | STAYS: order/derivation condition |\n| `tests/unit/workflow/test_executor_tripwire.py::test_executor_imports_no_scheduler_or_retry_lib`, `test_map_fanout_is_the_sole_concurrency_module` | asyncio/threading/retry libs banned in 2 files, required in 1 | STAYS: file-scoped ban + positive presence; TID251 is claimed |\n| `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/mutate/test_dependency_direction.py` (63) | reconciler imports only `ticket_reducer`/`event_append` engine seams | STAYS: bare engine names are legitimate elsewhere; TID251 claimed |\n| `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_neutrality.py`, `test_jira_family_boundary_heldout.py`, `test_rich_text_seam_heldout.py` ADF allowlists | scoped vendor-import bans with allowlists | STAYS: scoped, substring/AST-mixed, and the reconciler epic renames the package |\n\n### Exact TOML for `pyproject.toml`\n\nIn `[tool.ruff.lint]` `select` (`:462-486`), add the two codes:\n\n```toml\n    \"TID251\",\n    \"TID253\",\n```\n\nNew tables (placed after `[tool.ruff.lint]`, before `[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]`):\n\n```toml\n[tool.ruff.lint.flake8-tidy-imports]\nbanned-module-level-imports = [\n    \"langchain\",\n    \"langgraph\",\n    \"langchain_anthropic\",\n    \"langchain_openai\",\n    \"langchain_mcp_adapters\",\n    \"langfuse\",\n    \"anthropic\",\n    \"deepagents\",\n    \"opentelemetry\",\n    \"pydantic_ai\",\n    \"httpx\",\n    \"tree_sitter\",\n    \"tree_sitter_language_pack\",\n    \"hcl2\",\n    \"lark\",\n]\n\n[tool.ruff.lint.flake8-tidy-imports.banned-api]\n\"tests\".msg = \"tests.-rooted imports resolve only with the repo root on sys.path, which the bare pytest console script (make test, CI) does not provide; import same-directory helpers by bare name (bug a371)\"\n```\n\nIn `[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]`:\n\n```toml\n\"src/rebar/_engine/**\" = [\"TID253\"]\n\"tests/**\" = [\"T201\", \"TID253\"]      # was \"tests/**\" = [\"T201\"] at :536\n\"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\", \"TID253\"]    # was \"scripts/**\" = [\"T201\"] at :578\n```\n\nThe `\"src/rebar/_engine/**\"` key becomes `\"src/rebar/reconciler/**\"` if the reconciler epic (friended-brainsick-degus) lands its package move first; whichever change lands second updates the path.\n\n### RED proof (record the three transcripts as a comment on this ticket)\n\n```sh\nprintf 'from tests.unit.nothing import x\\n' > tests/unit/test_e10_red_tid251.py && ruff check tests/unit/test_e10_red_tid251.py\n# expected: one `TID251 \\`tests\\` is banned`\nprintf 'import httpx\\n' > src/rebar/_e10_red.py && ruff check src/rebar/_e10_red.py\n# expected: one `TID253 \\`httpx\\` is banned at the module level`\nprintf 'def f():\\n    import httpx\\n    return httpx\\n' > src/rebar/_e10_red.py && ruff check src/rebar/_e10_red.py\n# expected: clean\nrm tests/unit/test_e10_red_tid251.py src/rebar/_e10_red.py\n```"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788807459864148530,"uuid":"894db12b-a950-4bfd-b5a3-7e1266b8bb70"}